WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.120
The Lord of the Rings is a big deal.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:04.120
J.R.R.

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:08.170
Tolkien's epic fantasy created a genre, inspired
a series of hit movies, and singlehandedly

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:09.700
altered the economy of New Zealand.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:13.870
So you can imagine the excitement when HarperCollins
announced that Tolkien's spinoff story about

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:19.180
lovers Beren and Lúthien is to be published
as a standalone novel in 2017—exactly a

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:21.320
century after Tolkien started writing it.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:25.220
Here's everything you need to know about the
new Lord of the Rings spinoff.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:26.220
Son rise

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.220
J.R.R.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:31.060
Tolkien wrote numerous stories about the history
of Middle-earth, some of them incomplete or

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:32.189
contradictory.

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:35.649
After his death, Tolkien's son Christopher
edited a few of them into loose collections

00:00:35.649 --> 00:00:38.059
like Unfinished Tales and The Silmarillion.

00:00:38.059 --> 00:00:41.819
Beren and Lúthien is Christopher's second
attempt at editing some of his father's Middle-earth

00:00:41.819 --> 00:00:44.109
backstory into a standalone novel.

00:00:44.109 --> 00:00:49.100
The first was The Children of Húrin, a relentlessly
miserable tale about a family doomed by a

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.379
terrible curse.

00:00:50.379 --> 00:00:53.981
Fortunately, Beren and Lúthien is a lot more
upbeat, though exactly what will be in the

00:00:53.981 --> 00:00:56.089
book is a bit of a mystery.

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:59.979
Tolkien produced multiple versions of the
basic story, including a draft in which Sauron

00:00:59.979 --> 00:01:01.309
appears as an evil cat...

00:01:01.309 --> 00:01:08.240
...and an unfinished poem that suddenly cuts
off mid-werewolf attack.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:10.189
Lore of the rings

00:01:10.189 --> 00:01:13.759
Although Beren and Lúthien takes place in
the same world as The Hobbit and Lord of the

00:01:13.759 --> 00:01:17.350
Rings, it's set over 6,500 years earlier.

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:21.500
To put that in perspective, the land where
the story takes place sinks beneath the ocean

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:26.719
in a massive cataclysm about four millennia
before hobbits even appear as a species.

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:30.380
The world isn't even the same shape, since
a particularly angry god violently changes

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:32.880
it from flat to round between the two stories.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:36.780
In other words: you probably shouldn't expect
your favorite characters to pop in for a cameo.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.619
That said...

00:01:38.619 --> 00:01:40.210
Return of Sauron

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:44.729
The only character to appear in both Lord
of the Rings and Beren and Lúthien is Sauron,

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:47.310
who has the excuse of being immortal.

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:50.830
Interestingly, Sauron is essentially a second-tier
villain in Beren and Lúthien..

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:55.530
The real threat in the story is Sauron's boss,
a guy named Morgoth, the original dark lord

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:57.170
in Tolkien's mythology.

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:01.450
He's a being so powerful that a massive army
of angels eventually has to invade Middle-earth

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:03.280
to remove him from the picture.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:07.340
Even Sauron is terrified of him, and with
good reason — as the ultimate source of

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:11.860
evil, Morgoth was behind the creation of dragons,
orcs, werewolves, and trolls.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:17.099
He even boasts a personal bodyguard of balrogs,
each as powerful as the one that killed Gandalf

00:02:17.099 --> 00:02:18.500
that one time.

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:19.650
Personal story

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:23.409
Tolkien's wife Edith was the inspiration for
the beautiful Lúthien, whose songs enchant

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:27.069
Morgoth and move even the personification
of Death to tears.

00:02:27.069 --> 00:02:29.470
Edith met Tolkien when he was just 16.

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:35.110
His guardian forbade him to see her, but within
hours of turning 21, he proposed and she accepted.

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:38.020
Tolkien later wrote to his son Christopher
that the love story was:

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:42.300
"...first conceived in a small woodland glade
filled with hemlocks at Roos in Yorkshire.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:46.650
… In those days [Edith's] hair was raven,
her skin clear, her eyes brighter than you

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:49.360
have seen them, and she could sing—and dance."

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:53.610
The two were eventually buried together, sharing
a simple tombstone that bore the names "Beren"

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.330
and "Luthien."

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:57.049
Badass heroine

00:02:57.049 --> 00:03:00.560
One of the common criticisms of Lord of the
Rings and The Hobbit is that nearly all of

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:01.710
the heroes are men.

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:05.450
The book version of The Hobbit famously doesn't
have a single female character.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:09.930
Eowyn basically stands alone in the Lord of
the Rings books, although Peter Jackson expanded

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:14.629
Arwen's role for the movies, while he invented
Tauriel out of thin air.

00:03:14.629 --> 00:03:18.201
Beren and Lúthien seems like it's heading
in the same direction, when Lúthien's father

00:03:18.201 --> 00:03:21.099
gives Beren a quest to win his daughter's
hand in marriage.

00:03:21.099 --> 00:03:25.290
In a subversion, Beren and his all-male band
of companions fail catastrophically.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:29.780
Lúthien has to escape from her father and
personally face down Sauron to rescue her

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:31.790
warrior-in-distress from his dungeon.

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:36.110
For the rest of the story, she does all the
heavy lifting, successfully stealing a priceless

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:38.689
jewel from Morgoth while Beren tags along.

00:03:38.689 --> 00:03:42.829
Effectively, Lúthien takes matters into her
own hands and completes the quest herself

00:03:42.829 --> 00:03:45.660
to ensure she can marry the man she loves.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:47.189
Eagles to the rescue

00:03:47.189 --> 00:03:50.890
At a key point in the story, it seems certain
that Beren and Luthien are about to be captured

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:55.200
— and then three huge eagles swoop in out
of nowhere and carry them to safety.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:04:00.049
If that sounds familiar, it's because Tolkien
used the same plot device to save Bilbo and

00:04:00.049 --> 00:04:01.220
the dwarves in The Hobbit.

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:05.579
And then he used it again to save Sam and
Frodo at the end of Lord of the Rings.

00:04:05.579 --> 00:04:09.020
Thanks to Beren and Lúthien, we know the
eagles have been pulling this stunt for at

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:10.890
least 7,000 years.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:15.910
You'd think Sauron would forget invading Gondor
for a while and focus on killing these eagles,

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:21.080
since they're clearly evil's most persistent
enemy in Tolkien's continuity.

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:22.550
Cool new monsters

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:27.230
If you're bored with orcs and dragons, have
no fear: Beren and Lúthien introduces some

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:31.440
exciting new creatures to the world of Middle-earth,
including vampires and werewolves.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:36.540
"I was thinking maybe I should just bring
a broom down here for you if you wanted to

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:40.481
sweep up some of the skeletons."

00:04:40.481 --> 00:04:43.560
Unfortunately, the versions of the story that
have been published so far don't give us much

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:48.560
detail on what these creatures actually look
like, so no word yet whether or not Middle-earth

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:50.570
vampires sparkle.

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:52.910
The original Aragorn and Arwen

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:57.320
One aspect of the spinoff that should be familiar
to fans is the central love story.

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:02.940
Just like Aragorn and Arwen, Beren and Lúthien
are a mortal man and an immortal elf princess.

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:05.600
"You said you'd bind yourself to me.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:11.740
Forsaking the immortal life."

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:16.200
Like Arwen, Lúthien suspects the relationship
will cause her great sorrow, but she loves

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:18.700
Beren and can't bring herself to abandon him.

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:23.760
And, just like Elrond, Lúthien's father Thingol
is deeply opposed to the relationship.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:28.870
In fact, Aragorn is very aware of the parallels,
and repeatedly compares Arwen to Lúthien:

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:30.890
"Who is she?

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:34.250
This woman you sing of."

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:43.000
"Tis the Lay of Lúthien, the Elf-maiden who
gave her love to Beren."

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:47.850
In fact, Elrond and Arwen are Beren and Luthien's
descendants.

00:05:47.850 --> 00:05:52.520
That's why Arwen is able to choose to become
mortal at the end of Return of the King and

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:54.430
remain with Aragorn.

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:58.880
Luthien's sad song moved the godlike Valar
to let her become mortal so she and Beren

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:01.150
could be together even in death.

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:05.530
The Valar then allowed their half-elf, half-human
descendents to choose whether or not to be

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:09.060
mortal like humans or immortal like the elves.

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:13.690
While Elrond chose to become an elf, his daughter
made the choice of Luthien, becoming mortal

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:15.810
to stay with her one true love.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:18.590
"Some things are certain.

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:27.300
If I leave him now, I will regret it forever."

00:06:27.310 --> 00:06:31.760
Kinda makes your singing Valentine's Day card
seem pretty crappy by comparison, huh?

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:37.440
"I'm so excited and I just can't hide it."

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:42.380
"I'm about to lose control and I think I like
it."

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:44.630
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:46.840
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

